tau hy asya paripanthinau\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":1195,\"bb\":1061,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/34/b1061/\",\"shadow_value\":\"indriyasya – of the senses; indriyasya arthe – in the sense objects; rāga – attachment; dveṣau – also detachment; vyavasthitau – put under regulations; tayoḥ – of them; na – never; vaśam – control; āgacchet – one should come; tau – those; hi – certainly; asya – his; paripanthinau – stumbling blocks.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"indriyasya\",\"translation\":\"of the senses\"},{\"word\":\"indriyasya arthe\",\"translation\":\"in the sense objects\"},{\"word\":\"rāga\",\"translation\":\"attachment\"},{\"word\":\"dveṣau\",\"translation\":\"also detachment\"},{\"word\":\"vyavasthitau\",\"translation\":\"put under regulations\"},{\"word\":\"tayoḥ\",\"translation\":\"of them\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"vaśam\",\"translation\":\"control\"},{\"word\":\"āgacchet\",\"translation\":\"one should come\"},{\"word\":\"tau\",\"translation\":\"those\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"asya\",\"translation\":\"his\"},{\"word\":\"paripanthinau\",\"translation\":\"stumbling blocks\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":1196,\"bb\":1062,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/34/b1062/\",\"body_value\":\"There are principles to regulate attachment and aversion pertaining to the senses and their objects. One should not come under the control of such attachment and aversion, because they are stumbling blocks on the path of self-realization.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":1197,\"bb\":1063,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/3/34/b1063/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}